  1650	# Two DIFFERENT questions the gate answers, kept apart on purpose:
  1651	#
  1652	#   VERIFICATION  — "was this change actually checked?" tests bound to the config
  1653	#                   command, an independent diff review, a red-team at L3, every
  1654	#                   transcript hash-bound to the SHA. Machine-checkable evidence.
  1655	#   AUTHORIZATION — "did a human take responsibility for it?" the named approval
  1656	#                   the gate policy demands at L3.
  1657	#
  1658	# They are not interchangeable. The baseline walk asks only the FIRST question:
  1659	# a commit whose evidence VERIFIES is a sound place to start counting risk from,
  1660	# whether or not anyone signed for it — 238 fully-reviewed L3 commits across the
  1661	# fleet were never signed, and treating them as unreviewed collapsed every
  1662	# baseline to the root and inflated every floor to L3. The gate asks BOTH, and
  1663	# authorization is never inferred from verification: reviewers passing does not
  1664	# mean a human said yes.
  1665	def evaluate(report, tier, files, require_captured=False, root=None, test_command=None,
